{
  "_note": "Which places count as which city in the restaurant picker and the Guide (scripts/places_catalog.py). By default a place belongs to the nearest TripVibz city within the radius, which suits metro cities (Hollywood shows up under Fort Lauderdale). \"only\": islands and strictly defined cities list the address localities (Overture's spelling) that count as them; anything else nearby goes to the next city that will take it. \"also\": a city claims these localities even when another city's centre is nearer. \"exclude\": a city never takes these localities (a separate destination across the water or the county line); they go to the next city or nowhere. Places outside the US are never loaded. For an \"only\" city the loader prints the biggest localities it dropped, so a missing neighbourhood name shows up in the run log.",
  "miami-beach": {
    "only": [
      "Miami Beach"
    ]
  },
  "key-west": {
    "only": [
      "Key West",
      "Stock Island"
    ]
  },
